  (text "3. HOT-SIDE SUPPLY (LNK3204 HALF-WAVE BUCK, 5 V, THEN 3.3 V)" (at 21.5900 190.5000 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid bac8e870-e7cf-41e2-b162-9eb05f9d048c))
  (text "Replaces the KP3310 (R1 study, hardware/sim/R1-study.md): half-wave charging through a surge resistor could not supply the 8-15 mA load.\nHigh-side buck referenced to L_BUS. RF 47R + 2 x M7 + pi filter (2 x 4.7 uF 450 V, 1 mH): simulated bulk/drain peak 465 V at a 4 kV surge (switch\nrated 725 V).\nFeedback: C25 samples Vout during freewheel; 2.00 V x (1 + 3.09k/2.49k) = 4.48 V + about 0.5 V diode offset = 5.0 V (trim R35 at bring-up).\nBP/M = 1 uF selects the reduced current limit (enough for 20 mA, allows a small choke). D9 must be <= 35 ns trr (enclosure above 70 C)." (at 21.5900 194.3100 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 6c8bfebc-da9e-4866-ba3f-395c60e35871))
