  (rectangle (start 186.69 179.07) (end 410.21 295.91) (stroke (width 0.35) (type default)) (fill (type color) (color 214 92 64 0.10)) (uuid a8856c84-c9c6-468b-9d5b-17573a4e9054))
  (text "5. POLARITY AND EARTH CHECK (PULSE-WIDTH RATIO, S2 SCHEME F)" (at 187.9600 180.3400 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 56d2d98c-aa53-48e1-a3fd-d997d361f232))
  (text "Arm A: E -> 2 x 2M (HV) -> sense 47k -> L_BUS.  Arm B: E -> 2 x 2M (HV) + 47k -> N_F, so a missing earth floats to mid-supply.\nD3 (low leakage) passes the positive half-wave to R21; U4 compares it with 1.490 V (A) and 0.496 V (B). POL_A/POL_B are 50 Hz pulses.\nFirmware: duty d -> amplitude (TH/g + Vf)/cos(pi d), divided by the BL0939 mains peak, ratio to the unit's end-of-line k0:\n> 0.68 earthed and correct, 0.33-0.68 no earth (advisory, outlets empty only), < 0.33 swapped (outlets stay off). Run with relays open.\nEach arm must withstand a 6 kV impulse: VR37-class HV resistors." (at 187.9600 184.1500 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 32d69f55-2fd1-42bc-9d0b-585644bb5397))
